course: dictionary
lesson: 855
title: Between: the gap, the share, the link
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Between is a small word with a big job. Most of the time it means in the space in the middle of two things. «The ball is between the chairs» means the ball sits in the gap, with a chair on each side.
explain: Between also works with numbers and time. «Numbers between 10 and 20» are the ones bigger than 10 and smaller than 20. «Between 2 and 3 o'clock» is the time after 2 o'clock and before 3 o'clock.
explain: When things are shared, between means split among people. «The cake was shared between five children» means each child gets a fair part. A quick check: swap the word among into the sentence. If it still makes sense, between means shared out.
fact: Between means in the space in the middle of two things.
fact: Between can mean shared by two or more people, as in «split between the label, the songwriters and the artist».
fact: Between can mean the time from one thing to another, as in «counting the seconds between the flash and the bang».
fact: In numbers, between means bigger than one number and smaller than another: 5 is between 4 and 6.
fact: «Between you and me» means this is a secret, and «in between» means in the middle, neither one nor the other.
exercise: «Counting the seconds between the flash and the bang shows whether the storm is coming closer.» Here, between means | A place inside a box | *The time from the flash to the bang | Shared by two people | Very quick
exercise: Which number is between 4 and 6? | 9 | *5 | 2 | 7
exercise: «Split between the label, the songwriters and the artist» means | Forgotten by all of them | Thrown in the bin | *Shared out among them | Hidden from everyone
test: «A flask has two walls with almost no air between them.» Between here means | *In the space in the middle of two things | Very hot | Shared by two people | Bigger than one and smaller than two
test: Ben whispers, «Between you and me, Sam is moving house.» What does between you and me show? | A place to hide | *A secret that stays between two people | A time on a clock | A number in a sum
exam: In «the disparity between the two results», between shows | A time from one point to another | *A difference or gap between two things | A number bigger than one and smaller than another | Something shared out among people
